// ============================================================================
//  mod_freezefx.zone  -  the materials the ported wonder-weapon .efx need.
//
//  🛑 READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING ANYTHING HERE.
//
//  THE BUG THIS FIXES (user report 2026-08-14: "the winters howl is missing
//  visual effects when i shoot").
//
//  The .efx themselves were never the problem and are NOT missing - all 14
//  freeze effects have shipped as raw files in mod.iwd\fx\ since the port
//  landed, exactly as mod_wonderweapons.zone's header says (OAT cannot read or
//  write FxEffectDef, so an .efx can only travel raw). What was missing is the
//  MATERIALS those effects draw with.
//
//  An .efx is plain text (`iwfx 2`) and names its materials directly. Measured
//  by extracting every quoted "gfx_*" from all 14 and testing each against
//  (a) this mod.ff, (b) common_zm.ff / patch_zm.ff, (c) each map's own
//  fastfile, using a full 191-fastfile asset index:
//
//      Winter's Howl muzzle flash   4 of 8 materials unavailable on Diner
//      Tesla gun view fx            1 of 11  - and the tesla LOOKS FINE
//
//  That contrast is the diagnosis. A missing material does not kill the whole
//  effect, it kills the elements that use it - so the tesla survives losing one
//  and the Winter's Howl loses half its flash. 19 materials in total were
//  unreachable across the 14 effects; this file declares all 19.
//
//  🌟 EIGHT TECHNIQUESETS AND MOST IMAGES WERE ALREADY HERE. Only 11 images are
//  new. Checked one by one against the mod.ff asset dump - do not add
//  techniqueset lines here, mod_base.zone already carries every one of them
//  (effect_w77q49e8, effect_842ee834, particlecloud_w7046j83, effect_8f63534j,
//  effect_q01e8072, effect_50567j38, effect_3z0w0424, distortion_81587199).
//
//  WHERE THE ASSETS COME FROM
//
//  18 of the 19 resolve from zone_source\fx_donor\mod.ff - the fastfile of the
//  "T5 Winter's Howl Port" module that shipped these effects, which carries the
//  T5-matched copies. It is --load'ed LAST in build_ff.bat, so first-load-wins
//  means it can only ever supply a name that NO zombies fastfile above it
//  offers. Nothing shared changes owner. The 19th, gfx_fxt_bio_bloodtrail,
//  comes from so_zclassic_zm_buried.ff, which was already in the load list.
//
//  🛑 A FASTFILE CARRIES IMAGE HEADERS, NOT PIXELS. The 11 new images each have
//  their .iwi staged in zone_assets\images\, which build.bat copies into
//  images\ and pack_iwd.ps1 packs into mod.iwd. Remove one and that effect
//  draws black instead of not at all - which is worse. See CLAUDE.md §8.
// ============================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Images - the 11 that no fastfile this mod loads already carried.
//  Pixels: zone_assets\images\<name>.iwi, all from the donor's cmn_all.iwd so
//  header and payload are guaranteed to agree on format and dimensions.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
image,fxt_debris_ice
image,fxt_env_snow_flake_cloud_01
image,fxt_env_snow_flake_cloud_02
image,fxt_env_snow_flakes
image,fxt_env_water_droplets
image,fxt_env_water_plume_dense
image,fxt_fx_distortion_ring_warp
image,fxt_fx_distortion_shc_wave
image,fxt_fx_thundergun_ring
image,fxt_smk_swirl
image,fxt_smk_whisp_spiral

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Materials - the 19 the .efx ask for and could not reach.
//  Annotated with the effect that needs each, so a future reader can tell what
//  breaks if one is dropped.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

//  Winter's Howl MUZZLE FLASH (fx_freezegun_view / _world / _ug_view /
//  _ug_world). These four are the user-visible bug: half the flash.
material,gfx_fxt_fx_distortion_ring_warp
material,gfx_fxt_smk_whisp_spiral
material,gfx_fxt_env_snow_flakes
material,gfx_fxt_fx_thundergun_ring

//  Projectile trail (fx_trail_freezegun_geotail, fx_trail_freezegun_ring_emit)
material,gfx_fxt_env_water_droplets_add

//  Freeze-over on the zombie (fx_zombie_freeze_torso, fx_zombie_freeze_md)
material,gfx_fxt_smk_whisp_spiral_add
material,gfx_fxt_smk_whisp_spiral_add_z5
material,gfx_fxt_smk_whisp_spiral_z120

//  Shatter / crumple / ice chunks (fx_freezegun_shatter, fx_freezegun_crumple,
//  fx_freezegun_crumple_ice)
material,gfx_fxt_debris_gib_ice
material,gfx_fxt_debris_fine_clump
material,gfx_fxt_env_water_mist
material,gfx_fxt_fx_distortion_shc_wave
material,gfx_fxt_smk_spiral
material,gfx_fxt_smk_tendril_add

//  Upgraded impact explosion (fx_exp_freezegun_impact)
material,gfx_fxt_env_snow_flake_cloud_01_top
material,gfx_fxt_env_snow_flake_cloud_02_top
material,gfx_fxt_env_water_plume_dense_add
material,gfx_fxt_env_water_plume_dense_z120_gr

//  Blood streak trail (fx_trail_freezegun_blood_streak). The only one NOT from
//  the fx donor - so_zclassic_zm_buried.ff has it, and its image
//  fxt_bio_bloodtrail was already in mod.ff.
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodtrail

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  📝 ONE IMAGE ARRIVES WITHOUT BEING DECLARED HERE: fxt_smk_tendril.
//  gfx_fxt_smk_tendril_add (resolved from zm_tomb) references it, so the Linker
//  pulls its header in and mod.ff now owns that name on every map. It is a
//  stock image, so its pixels would come from the game's .ipak anyway - but its
//  .iwi is staged in zone_assets\images\ alongside the other eleven so the
//  header and the pixels are guaranteed to be the same copy. Verified by the
//  before/after asset audit: 4,829 -> 4,860, 31 added, ZERO removed, nothing
//  changed owner.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  v2.14.12 (2026-09-07) - THE SECOND SWEEP: every raw .efx the four wonder
//  weapons can actually REACH, re-measured.
//
//  Method: roots = every loadfx() in the 4 server modules + the 3 client
//  modules (stock common_zm's _zm_weap_thundergun.csc included, since that is
//  what the client really runs) + every fx field of the 12 weapon defs; then
//  the nested-effect closure through the .efx text. 42 of the 64 raw files are
//  reachable; the other 22 are BO1 leftovers nothing references. Every quoted
//  gfx_* in the 42 was resolved against mod.ff + all 32 zombies fastfiles,
//  per map. 64 of 71 resolved everywhere. These are the 7 that did not.
//
//  🛑 THE ONE THAT IS NOT A DONOR COPY: gfx_fxt_thundergun_view_glow.
//  It draws the glowing power cells on the Thundergun view model (2 of the 4
//  elements in each fx_thundergun_power_cell_view1/2/3). It exists in NO
//  fastfile this project loads and in no stock zombies zone at all - BO1's own
//  zombie_theater.ff carries it, and the T5 port never brought it over, so
//  the bulbs have been drawing without their glow sprite since v1.69.0. The
//  material JSON is an Unlinker dump out of Logo2K's T6 Thundergun module
//  (T6-Declassified-Public\mods\zm_t6_t6d_module_t5_wpn_zmb_thundergun\mod.ff)
//  - a T6 asset, not a T5 one - and its techset effect_8f63534j is stock
//  (common_zm). Pixels: fxt_zombie_thundergun_view_glow.iwi from that same
//  module's mod.iwd (IWi v27, 256x128, byte-identical to the copy in
//  Wonder_Weapons-T6ZM\src\images - two independent sources agree).
//
//  The other six resolve from fastfiles already on the --load list, with the
//  usual first-load-wins: gfx_fxt_smk_gen_vm / _z200 are stock names, so a
//  stock map's copy wins (highrise / prison) and the fx donor only fills in
//  where no stock zone above it has them. Their image fxt_smk_gen is
//  common_zm's - pixels in the game's own ipak on every map, so NOT staged
//  (staging a stock smoke texture into mod.iwd would override it for every
//  stock effect that uses it - CLAUDE.md, mod.iwd is search-path rank 1).
//  Same for fxt_bio_bloodburst_c / fxt_bio_bloodgush (common_zm). Only
//  fxt_bio_blood_cloud is not a stock image; its .iwi comes from the fx
//  donor's own cmn_all.iwd, the same origin as the header (md5 27201cca... =
//  zm_t6_t6d_module_t5_wpn_zmb_freezegun, measured).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

//  Thundergun power cells - the glow sprite (fx_thundergun_power_cell_view1/2/3)
image,fxt_zombie_thundergun_view_glow
material,gfx_fxt_thundergun_view_glow

//  Thundergun steam vents on fire (fx_thundergun_steam_view) - was absent on
//  TranZit, Nuketown and Mob; only Die Rise carried it.
material,gfx_fxt_smk_gen_vm

//  Thundergun muzzle smoke cloud (fx_thundergun_smoke_cloud) - absent on
//  Nuketown only.
material,gfx_fxt_smk_gen_z200

//  Winter's Howl gib burst (fx_flesh_gib_fatal_01, loadfx'd by both halves).
//  The shatter/crumple path that plays it needs the zm_death_freeze_t5
//  animstate, which no stock aitype carries (mod_wonderweapons.zone, v2.10.6),
//  so today this is a loaded-but-unplayed effect; declared so it is complete.
image,fxt_bio_blood_cloud
material,gfx_fxt_bio_blood_cloud
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodburst_c
material,gfx_fxt_bio_bloodgush
